<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM2-WINDOWS-CFG-UNIX-COMPILE-BREAK>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM2-WINDOWS-CFG-UNIX-COMPILE-BREAK" ;
  triage:title "atm-daemon-client fails to compile on Windows: PathBuf import is gated #[cfg(unix)] but PathBuf is used unconditionally throughout the file" ;
  triage:description "Commit 4a35fa18 (AM.2's raw-framing deletion) introduced 'use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};' gated behind '#[cfg(unix)]' near the top of crates/atm-daemon-client/src/lib.rs. PathBuf is used unconditionally elsewhere in the same file (DaemonLocalIpcEndpoint, DaemonBinaryPath, host_local_http_record_path, ensure_daemon_available_with_lock_path_impl's launch_lock_path parameter, try_acquire_at, plus the #[cfg(test)] module) -- none of those call sites are themselves unix-gated. Confirmed via live CI: PR #833 job 'Test (windows-latest)' (run 31426740607, job 93580391167) fails with real rustc E0425 errors ('cannot find type PathBuf in this scope' at lib.rs:633, plus siblings), not a flake -- confirmed by fetching the actual job log via gh api. This directly violates the repo's mandatory Windows CI compliance patterns (docs/cross-platform-guidelines.md, cited as required reading in CLAUDE.md). None of the 6 dispatched reviewer agents caught this since they run on macOS/Linux; caught only by quality-mgr directly monitoring `gh pr checks` per the dispatch's own workflow step (j). RECHECK (QA-AM2-2, 2026-08-10, commit fab8bdbe): FIXED. Commit 5952dcb5 removed the #[cfg(unix)] gate from the PathBuf import; PR #833's 'Test (windows-latest)' job (run 31428312920, job 93585505085) now passes -- confirmed live via `gh pr checks 833 --watch`, not assumed. Independently confirmed by all 4 QA-2 reviewers (req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, rust-qa-agent) plus quality-mgr's own direct read of the current import line. Note: fixing this compile break unmasked a second, pre-existing latent bug (unrelated to AM.2, last touched by commit 780a8870) -- an unconditional import of LocalDaemonTransport in the same file's test module whose only usage is inside a #[cfg(unix)] test, causing 'Just lint (windows-latest)' to now fail on '-D unused-imports'. Filed separately as AM2-WINDOWS-LINT-UNUSED-IMPORT since it is a distinct symbol/root cause, not a regression of this fix." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "cross-platform" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-10T20:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-10T20:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AM-S2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-10T20:02:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
